    content: "# Game Title Screen, HUD, Game Shell & Gameplay Craft\n\nRead and apply these rules whenever the user request involves a 2D or 3D game.\n(If the game uses Three.js / WebGL or 3D graphics, also read\n[references/games_3d.md](references/games_3d.md).)\n\n> **Precedence over Website Chrome**: Full-viewport games use a **Game Shell**\n> (`Title Screen` -> `Playing HUD` -> `Pause / Victory / Game Over` modal) \342\200\224\n> **never** render a website `<header>` navigation bar, nav links, or marketing\n> footer on a game, and **never** use CSS `backdrop-filter` / `backdrop-blur`\n> over active WebGL or Canvas2D viewports.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n## Part I: Landing Page & Title Screen Craft\n\nThe landing screen sets the emotional stakes of the game in the first 500ms.\nBefore writing code, choose a **Start-Screen Stage, Layout & Title Lockup**\nsuited to your game\'s genre, setting, and art direction, and note your choice in\nyour verification plan:\n\n### 1. Choose One Stage Approach\n\n1.  **Live World Camera Tour / Parallax Pan** (*best for 3D spatial worlds,\n    racing, flight, open arenas, or multi-plane 2D environments*):\n    -   Drive `camera.position` and `camera.lookAt` along a smooth spline\n        flyover (3D) or multi-plane parallax pan (2D) populated with ambient\n        world motion (idling actors/vehicles, swaying foliage, drifting\n        particles) while keeping the player invulnerable and gameplay HUD bars\n        hidden.\n    -   When `[data-start]` is triggered, smoothly interpolate (`damp`) or cut\n        to the gameplay camera rig and reset local camera offsets/rotations to\n        `(0, 0, 0)` once in `\'playing\'`.\n2.  **Interactive Centerpiece / Hero Showcase** (*best for games built around an\n    iconic vehicle, hero subject, board/card table, or tactile physics/shader\n    centerpiece*):\n    -   Stage the hero 3D mesh, focal subject, or interactive artifact in the\n        focal region with immediate pre-start cursor feedback (parallax tilt,\n        gaze tracking, or turntable spin), transitioning directly into the\n        active arena on Start.\n3.  **Diegetic In-World Awakening** (*best for character-led adventures,\n    platformers, or stealth games*):\n    -   Frame the protagonist in a resting pose inside Stage 1 beside a\n        signature prop with gameplay HUD hidden. On Start, advance the character\n        into their ready stance while dissolving title elements and damping the\n        camera into gameplay framing without a scene cut.\n4.  **Illustrated Key-Art Backdrop (`generate_image`)** (*best for narrative,\n    RPG, fantasy, or atmospheric 2D games where bespoke key art sets world\n    identity*):\n    -   Call `generate_image` (`AspectRatio: \"16:9\"`, `ImageName: \"title_bg\"`)\n        with an explicit medium (e.g., *gouache painting, cel-shaded key art,\n        woodblock print*), lighting, palette, **30%-40% low-detail negative\n        space** (sky, deep shadow, or fog) for typography, and **\"no text, no\n        letters, no logos, no UI\"**.\n\n### 2. Compositional Layout, `<svg>` Title Emblem & Start Handshake\n\n1.  **Negative-Space Composition**:\n    -   Anchor the focal subject and the title/CTA in complementary regions so\n        text sits strictly over **30%-40% calm negative space** (asymmetric\n        left/right third split, centered monument spotlight with upper/lower\n        negative space, or framed inset vignette) with generous safe margins.\n2.  **Custom Inline `<svg>` Title Lockup & Clean Control Hint**:\n    -   Craft a bespoke inline `<svg>` title emblem or display lockup matched to\n        the game\'s world (crest emblem, poster lockup, diegetic world-material\n        plaque, or silhouette-integrated lettering) paired with a clear primary\n        Start CTA (`<= 3` menu actions total).\n    -   Format non-interactive control hints (`WASD Move \302\267 Space Jump \302\267 Esc\n        Pause`) as a single flat, borderless inline line in the bottom safe\n        margin. Omit SaaS eyebrow pill badges, pre-title kickers, multi-line\n        lore paragraphs, and CSS `linear-gradient` text/button fills.\n3.  **Title-to-Start Handshake**:\n    -   Attach `data-start=\"true\"` to the primary clickable start button/prompt,\n        support `?autostart=1` to skip directly to `\'playing\'`, **and** bind\n        `Enter` and `Space` while in `\'title\'` to trigger the same start\n        handler.\n    -   Triggering Start must immediately (`t = 0ms`) set\n        `document.body.dataset.state = \'playing\'`, hide the title overlay, blur\n        any focused DOM button, and begin gameplay.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n## Part II: HUD Visual Coherence, Gaze Routing & Game Shell Architecture\n\nThe HUD and game shell must feel **visually and materially native to the game\'s\nworld**, route indicators by **player gaze frequency**, convey **only live\nmechanics-backed state**, and keep **at least 85% of the viewport unobstructed\nin spatial action/board games**.\n\n### 1. World-Matched HUD Craft & Genre-Adaptive Topology\n\n1.  **World-Matched Framing Over Generic SaaS Chrome**:\n    -   Shape and tint every HUD element from the game world\'s own material,\n        palette, and lighting register rather than generic web cards\n        (`bg-slate-900/80 rounded-xl`) or `1px solid` boxes of uniform `text-xs`\n        labels.\n2.  **Genre-Adaptive Shell Topology**:\n    -   *Real-Time Action, Platformer, Shooter, Flight & Racing Games*: Keep the\n        viewport full-bleed with **`<= 2-3` compact perimeter corner clusters**\n        (plus on-character/companion cues where appropriate) and keep the\n        central playfield (`35%` to `65%` X/Y) clear of persistent chrome.\n    -   *Grid, Puzzle, Board, Card & Tower-Defense Games*: Anchor tools,\n        buildable selection cards, and counters into a **single unified\n        perimeter dock/strip** framing the board without overlapping interactive\n        tiles.\n    -   *Narrative, Interactive Fiction & Management/Sim Games*: Compose a\n        cohesive atmospheric scene window, spatial map or node graph, and\n        balanced editorial reading/choice panels (`55-75ch`).\n3.  **Hero-to-Kicker Typographic Hierarchy (`~2.5:1-3:1` Scale & Tabular\n    Numerals)**:\n    -   Render primary readouts (`Vitality Pips`, `Score / Combo`, `Speed`, `Lap\n        / Position`, `Wave`, `Currency`, `Moves`) as prominent graphical pips or\n        display numerals (`font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`, outer\n        stroke/shadow `paint-order: stroke fill`), paired with compact uppercase\n        kicker labels (`HP`, `WAVE`, `SCRAP`, `SPEED`) at `~1/3` the hero scale.\n    -   Format all HUD numbers as integers via `Math.round()` or `.toFixed(0)`\n        (use `.toFixed(1)` only for sub-second cooldown timers).\n4.  **Code-Authored `<svg>` HUD Icons, Vitality Sockets & Rally Bars**:\n    -   Author HUD icons, vitality sockets, reticles, and ability slots in\n        inline `<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">` or `<canvas>` with a **dark outer\n        silhouette**, **interior structural detail**, and **top highlight +\n        state fill**, matching each HUD icon\'s silhouette and accent hue 1-to-1\n        with its in-world pickup or prop.\n    -   Render discrete health/charge pips with 3 readable states (**Full**,\n        **Damaged/Cracked**, and **Empty Hollow Socket**), and give continuous\n        health/stamina bars a delayed trailing damage/drain ghost bar.\n5.  **Live Mechanics Parity, Equipment Clarity & Gaze Routing**:\n    -   Every HUD counter, meter, or `[Key]` badge must connect to live gameplay\n        producers/consumers and active event listeners. When the player selects\n        among multiple weapons, abilities, or buildable towers/units, show each\n        option\'s **live stock/cost, `[Key]` binding, and concise Name +\n        Role/Effect clue** (e.g., `Rotary Turret \302\267 Rapid Single-Target`).\n    -   **Gaze Routing**: Place fast-depleting ability timers/ammo cues near the\n        character or exact `(0, 0)` center crosshair (`position: fixed; left:\n        50%; top: 50%; pointer-events: none`), use a subtle peripheral screen\n        vignette at critical low HP, project real navigable level geometry onto\n        any corner minimap, and guard 3D world-to-screen projections with\n        `v.z >= -1 && v.z <= 1`.\n    -   Render top-right utility controls (`Mute [M]`, `Pause [P]`, `Restart\n        [R]`) as compact clickable square `<svg>` icon buttons with\n        `tabIndex={-1}` and `e.currentTarget.blur()` wired to both click and\n        keyboard listeners.\n\n### 2. React <-> 60 FPS Simulation Decoupling & Pointer Pass-Through\n\n1.  **Decouple React Reconciliation from the `60 Hz` Loop**:\n    -   Mount the `<canvas>` / Three.js renderer inside an isolated sibling\n        `<div ref={mountRef} />` outside re-rendering HUD components. Mutate\n        high-frequency bars/timers via DOM refs\n        (`barRef.current.style.transform`) or throttle React state updates to\n        discrete integer/phase changes.\n2.  **Pointer Pass-Through & Zero-Filter Compositing**:\n    -   Set `pointer-events: none` on full-viewport HUD wrappers (`fixed\n        inset-0`) and `pointer-events: auto` only on interactive buttons, slots,\n        and modal cards.\n    -   Style HUD surfaces using `rgba(...)` fills, `box-shadow`, `text-shadow`,\n        and `<svg>` paths \342\200\224 never `backdrop-filter` / `backdrop-blur` over a\n        live canvas.\n\n### 3. Complete Game State Machine & Outcome-Matched Status Modals\n\nMirror the game state machine to `document.body.dataset.state` (`\'title\'`,\n`\'playing\'`, `\'paused\'`, `\'gameover\'`):\n\n1.  **Transition Hygiene**:\n    -   On `VICTORY` or `GAME_OVER`, freeze an immutable snapshot of end-of-run\n        stats (`score`, `best`, `wave/time/progress`) before resetting state,\n        after a brief `0.4-0.7s` final beat on defeat.\n    -   On entering `\'playing\'`, blur active DOM buttons, focus the canvas, and\n        clear held inputs (`keysPressed.clear()`, `mouseDown = false`). Exit\n        PointerLock (`document.exitPointerLock?.()`) on `\'paused\'`,\n        `\'gameover\'`, or `\'title\'`. Lock unreached stages (`disabled={stageIdx >\n        highestReachedStage}`) on any stage selector.\n2.  **Single Focused Status Modal Card**:\n    -   Render **one focused modal card** per status state (`Pause`, `Victory`,\n        `Game Over`) in the world\'s typography and palette with `2-3`\n        `tabular-nums` stat tiles and primary action CTAs:\n\nState                     | `document.body.dataset.state` | Required Behavior & Modal Content\n:------------------------ | :---------------------------- | :--------------------------------\n**Title**                 | `\'title\'`                     | Boots into `\'title\'` (unless `?autostart=1` is set). Primary CTA has `data-start=\"true\"`; `Enter`/`Space` also starts.\n**Playing**               | `\'playing\'`                   | Active simulation + world-matched HUD (`>= 85%` clear viewport in action/board games).\n**Paused**                | `\'paused\'`                    | Triggered by **`Escape` or `P`** (or Pause button). Exits PointerLock, freezes simulation, silences audio loops, and shows Pause modal (`Resume`, `Restart`, `Title`).\n**Victory / Stage Clear** | `\'gameover\'`                  | Freezes run snapshot, plays fanfare, and shows Victory modal with **Mastery Metrics** (`Clear Time`, `Score / Best`, `Damage Taken` or `Objectives X/Y`) + **Play Again / Next Stage (`data-start=\"true\"`)**.\n**Game Over (Defeat)**    | `\'gameover\'`                  | Freezes run snapshot, exits PointerLock, plays defeat sting, and shows Game Over modal with **Progress-Toward-Goal Metrics** (`Wave / Stage / Distance Reached`, `Boss HP Remaining`, `Score / Best`) + **Try Again (`data-start=\"true\"`)**.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n## Part III: Core Gameplay Loop, Responsive Controls, Animation & Encounter Design\n\n### 1. Clamped Simulation Step, Hitstop, Weight-Scaled Juice & Pooled Particles\n\n1.  **Clamped `dt` (`Math.min(rawDt, 0.05)`) & Sim-Level Hitstop**:\n    -   Clamp frame `dt` to `<= 0.05s` so tab switches or frame hiccups never\n        tunnel fast entities through walls.\n    -   Advance gameplay physics using `simDt = dt * timeScale` with a real\n        `hitstop` freeze timer (`0.03-0.08s` on heavy hits, parries, boss phase\n        breaks, and kills) where rendering, hit flashes, and camera shake\n        continue ticking in real `dt` while simulation physics pause.\n2.  **Weight-Scaled Multi-Channel Juice**:\n    -   Every core player verb (jump, land, shoot/swing, hit enemy, kill, take\n        damage, pickup, dash) must trigger synchronized visual + procedural Web\n        Audio feedback scaled to event weight:\n        -   *Light events* (footstep, jump, light shot, pickup): pitch-varied\n            (`\302\2618%`) procedural synth + subtle squash/recoil + `3-6` directional\n            particles.\n        -   *Heavy events* (heavy hit, kill, explosion, player hurt): `40-60ms`\n            white/emissive hit flash on the target, `0.03-0.08s` sim hitstop,\n            directional knockback impulse, decaying `trauma * trauma` camera\n            shake, and a `12-28` particle burst.\n3.  **Zero-GC Pooled Particle Ring Buffer**:\n    -   Pre-allocate a fixed-capacity particle pool (typed arrays, a fixed\n        object ring buffer, or a single `THREE.InstancedMesh`) updated in-place\n        each frame; never allocate and garbage-collect new particle or vector\n        objects inside `requestAnimationFrame`.\n\n### 2. Unified Input Hygiene, Edge Triggers, Coyote/Buffering & Viewport Aiming\n\n1.  **Edge-Triggered One-Shots vs. Held Intents**:\n    -   Track both continuous `held` states and single-frame `justPressed` edges\n        in a unified input hub. One-shot actions (Jump, single-shot Attack,\n        Dash, Interact, Pause) must consume `justPressed` so holding a key never\n        auto-bunny-hops or machine-guns on every frame.\n2.  **Input Buffering, Coyote Time & Variable Jump Cut**:\n    -   In platformers and action games, buffer Jump/Dash/Attack inputs for\n        `0.10-0.14s` before landing or cooldown completion so slightly early\n        presses fire on the first legal frame, grant `0.08-0.12s` **coyote\n        time** after leaving a ledge, and cut upward velocity (`vy *= 0.45`)\n        when Jump is released early while ascending.\n3.  **Focus-Loss Key Release & Live `ResizeObserver` World Projection**:\n    -   Clear all held keys and mouse buttons (`keysPressed.clear()`,\n        `mouseDown = false`) on `window` `blur` and `document`\n        `visibilitychange` so keys never stick (do **not** auto-open the\n        `\'paused\'` modal on `window` `blur`, which would block headless browser\n        verification captures).\n    -   Convert pointer coordinates to world space through a single\n        `screenToWorld(clientX, clientY)` helper backed by live\n        `getBoundingClientRect()` / `ResizeObserver` canvas bounds \342\200\224 never\n        hardcode viewport dimensions (`1280x800`).\n\n### 3. Movement Feel, Attack Curves & KO Transitions\n\n1.  **Squash-and-Stretch, Gait Sync & Readable Attack Curves**:\n    -   Sync movement bob or walk cycles to distance traveled rather than fixed\n        frame counters so actors never appear to skate when decelerating, and\n        apply subtle squash-and-stretch on jump takeoff (`scaleX: 0.85, scaleY:\n        1.18`) and landing (`scaleX: 1.22, scaleY: 0.78`, exponentially damped\n        back to `1`).\n    -   Structure melee and projectile attacks with distinct **windup -> active\n        -> recovery** phases, and give defeated enemies a `0.25-0.5s` **KO\n        topple, knockback arc, or dissolve transition** rather than splicing\n        them out of the actor list on the exact frame `hp <= 0`.\n\n### 4. Enemy Archetype Diversity, Attack Telegraphs & Fair Difficulty Ramp\n\n1.  **`>= 3` Distinct Enemy Movement & Behavior Policies**:\n    -   Action games with enemies must implement at least **3 genuinely distinct\n        movement/decision policies** (e.g., *Chaser/Swarmer*, *Kiter/Ranged*,\n        *Line-of-Sight Charger*, *Orbiter/Flanker*, *Area-Denial Turret*,\n        *Shielded Front*) with distinct silhouettes and palettes \342\200\224 never spawn\n        multiple enemy types that all execute the same `position +=\n        normalize(player - pos) * speed` seek loop.\n2.  **Visible + Audible Attack Telegraphs & Crowd Token Pool**:\n    -   Any enemy or hazard attack that deals `> 10%` of max player HP must\n        display a **`0.25-0.8s` visual and audio windup telegraph** (crouch or\n        emissive flash, ground target ring, aim sight line, rising pitch cue)\n        before the active hitbox frames, and limit simultaneous crowd attacks\n        via an **attack token pool** (`2-5` concurrent attackers) so large waves\n        stay readable and fair.\n3.  **Multi-Knob Difficulty Ramp & Genre-Native Loss Reachability**:\n    -   Scale challenge across play time using at least 3 knobs (spawn budget,\n        archetype mix, hazard density, speed/aggression) while keeping the\n        opening `10-15s` approachable.\n    -   Match loss conditions to the genre: combat and arcade games use\n        reachable HP/hazard defeat (never clamp player HP with a hidden\n        `Math.max(1, hp)` floor or permanent invulnerability), racing/sports\n        games use placement or timer finish rather than instant crash-death, and\n        cozy/creative or pure logic puzzle games keep failure optional or\n        undoable.\n"
    num_lines: 280
    num_bytes: 17526
    line_range_bytes: 17526
  }
}
