  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Deobfuscated Constants**\n\nI\'ve successfully extracted and verified the deobfuscated constants from the live production bundles of `https://longhoang-lyo.com/`. I\'m now meticulously reviewing all the data, with the first item on the list being the Camera module, identified as `CQl67Veh.`.\n\n\n**Examining Camera Parameters**\n\nI\'ve been deeply focused on the camera module (`CQl67Veh`) constants, specifically the perspective camera configuration. I\'ve noted the isometric-like 35\302\260 FOV and its pseudo-orthographic alternative. The `Vector3` angle data is next; I have extracted default and specific configurations, and I\'ve analyzed the zoom parameters and the follow damping mechanism; it looks like a critically damped second-order spring, parameterized by `smoothTime`, and dependent on player speed via `speedAlpha`. Mouse pan and recoil constants are also in scope now.\n\n\n**Investigating Tank Control**\n\nI\'ve moved on to examining the tank/robot controller and its associated Rapier physics, focusing on the `B1Nq4Kq6.js` module. I am analyzing the gravity parameters, fixed timestep, and maximum physics steps, as well as the initialization parameters for the robot\'s rigidbody, cuboid collider properties, and model scale. The tank\'s drive kinematics and control parameters are also under scrutiny, including speeds, rotation rates, and damping factors.\n\n\n**Delving into Bullet Physics**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the bullet and recoil mechanics. I\'m focusing on the `ci` module, unpacking cannon-related constants. I\'ve dissected the fire rate, projectile speed, and life span, then I moved onto analyzing the recoil constants, like durations, distances, and angles for both visual and physical effects. The bullet light parameters are also on my list. Finally, I\'m analyzing the bullet impact behavior on props, including impulse and torque.\n\n\n**Unpacking Telekinesis & Assets**\n\nI\'ve moved on to examining the physics grab mode, and I\'m currently unpacking the parameters for telekinesis in the Factory Playground. I have the holding distance, spring strength, damping, and acceleration, as well as angular acceleration parameters for this mode. I am now working on understanding how these values affect the player\'s ability to manipulate objects. Next, I\'m analyzing the hover outline visuals, including stroke color and width. Finally, I\'m reviewing the 3D asset manifest, specifically the robot, bullet models, zone and static and dynamic props.\n\n\n\n**Analyzing Asset Properties**\n\nI\'ve transitioned to the analysis of static props and collectibles, starting with props: I\'m examining the properties of the `TrafficCone`, `WheelBarrow`, `WoodenBox`, and `Bench` assets. Following that, I\'ll review the `Circuit`, `Fuel`, `Gear`, and `Tools` collectibles.\n\n\n\n**Exploring Visual Effects**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the visual effects, starting with the environment lighting constants for different times of day: dusk, night, and dawn. I\'m focusing on the light and shadow colors, as well as fog colors. Next, I\'m examining the cartoon puff smoke properties; I\'m analyzing spawn radius, velocity, lifespan, scale, opacity, and sway.\n\n\n**Defining Application Requirements**\n\nI\'m now outlining the application\'s core functionality. I will create a full-viewport, 1:1 interactive 3D WebGL clone of the \"LYOOO PORTFOLIO / Factory Playground.\" This will include implementing the Polygon/Hexagon Cutout Viewport on the right. The application will support title and playing states, with auto-start and start button triggers.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Experience**\n\nI am now outlining the visual design of the Factory Playground clone. I\'ve specified a cel-shaded, neon-green tank with dark outlines. I\'ve designed the title lockup, button placements and behaviors, and an initial hexagon cutout expanding to full-screen. I\'ve also detailed the interactive elements of the playground, including props, collectibles, and enemy robot types.\n\n\n**Designing Report Accessibility**\n\nI\'m now focusing on accessibility and the user experience. I\'ve decided to implement a dedicated \"REA Report & Roblox Luau Studio\" modal, triggered by a button in the top-right HUD and the Title Screen. Within this modal, I\'m designing three tabs for comprehensive data access: Tab 1 will provide a complete mathematical constants table, including camera vectors, physics constants, and shader data; Tab 2 will contain a complete, ready-to-use Luau script for the isometric camera; and Tab 3 will feature scripts for the tank builder and controller.\n\n\n"
