    thinking: "**Analyzing the Request**\n\nOkay, I\'m carefully dissecting the user\'s request, focusing on the game\'s transformation within `/src/game/FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx` and `/src/App.tsx`, and how it links to the Luau scripts. I\'m aiming to fully grasp the scope and implications.\n\n\n**Defining Player Actions**\n\nI\'ve shifted my focus to the player\'s interactions. The primary character is \"Buddy,\" a blocky avatar, not a tank. I\'m visualizing the core mechanics: running with animated limbs, aiming with the mouse, and weapon handling like an Uzi or Katana. I\'m exploring the physical cycle of grabbing crates, hoisting them overhead, and throwing them onto the stacking pad. I\'m also planning the removal of the old UI crate stacking system.\n\n\n**Visualizing Gameplay Actions**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the in-game mechanics. I can clearly picture \"Buddy\" hoisting a 3D crate above his head, running it towards the base. At each base, I\'ve envisioned a 3D Stacking Pad. Pressing \'E\' near the pad will result in a parabolic throw, stacking the crates in a 3D grid, complete with a hologram preview. Additionally, I\'m defining that pressing \'F\' near a crate outside the pad results in Health and Ammo drops, and \'F\' near the stack can spawn weapons or AI characters.\n\n\n**Envisioning New Spawnable Items**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific in-game item spawns based on crate stacking configurations. I see a rotating **Shotgun/Ice Gun/Laser Rifle**, automatically picked up. Two horizontal crates spawn grenades or cluster bombs and ammo. Two vertical crates spawn a new AI Buddy unit with different classes. Four horizontal crates reveal heavy weapons like a Bazooka, and four vertical spawn Tier 2 AI Buddies. Finally, eight full cube crates spawn a green and yellow Lyo Tank, or a Super Dual-Cannon Tyrant Tank if blue crates are present. There\'s also an empty Lyo Tank for player mounting near the blue base.\n\n\n**Implementing Tank Interactions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on tank-related interactions. I\'ve designed the mount/dismount mechanics. I\'ll make mounting the empty Lyo Tank using **`[G]` or `[E]`**, causing the character to pop up inside the open turret, and moving the character\'s head and upper body to reflect the turret\'s rotation. Dismounting via **`[G]`** returns the character to its normal state. Additionally, the tank can now run over crates, automatically picking up to four at a time and dropping them at the stacking pad.\n\n\n\n**Designing the Landscape**\n\nI\'m now visualizing the map\'s visual elements. I see the main path as a warm orange (`#d89c60`) with a darker border (`#c28348`). This path connects the Blue Base (South) and Red Base (North) to the Central and Side Drop Zones. I\'m imagining hundreds of 3D grass blades (`#6cd938`) swaying in the wind, along with small yellow-purple flowers and blue-purple leaf trees (`#1d1f8c` canopy + `#8c4a27` trunk) that break into Power-Ups on impact!\n\n\n**Defining Squad Mechanics**\n\nI\'m now focusing on squad control. I need to define command options such as \"HARVEST,\" \"ATTACK,\" \"DEFEND,\" and \"FOLLOW.\" I\'m reviewing `/src/game/rules.ts` to implement a helper for automated slot selection within the Stacking Pad, dependent on the Build Recipe target (using \'Q\'). I\'m checking how the `chooseNextPadSlotIndex` function manages slot assignment based on the target build order, specifically for vertical and horizontal configurations.\n\n\n"
