  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating Workflow Sequence**\n\nI\'m making sure to execute the standard workflow sequence: build, test, compile, restart the dev server, then Playwright verification with screenshot inspection. I\'m actively following `ultra-mode` and will adapt as necessary.\n\n\n**Analyzing New Feature Requests**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of the feature requests. I\'m focusing on the \"Clean Match Start\" enhancement. I\'m taking notes on how `bluePadSlots` and `redPadSlots` should be initialized, making sure there are no parked tanks at the start. I\'m checking the initial states for tanks and HUD elements. Also, I\'m setting an intention to modify the App.tsx file.\n\n\n**Defining Build Order Patterns**\n\nI\'m now nailing down the build order patterns, specifically for the `[Q]` key cycling. I\'m focusing on supporting all six explicit patterns within `BuildOrderTarget`, and cycling directly through them. I\'m keeping the default as `\'1x1x2\'` (Buddy T1) or `\'2x2x2\'`. I\'m also considering the compatibility with existing unit tests with `\'AUTO\'` and adding new ones.\n\n\n**Implementing Slot Enforcement**\n\nI\'m now implementing strict slot enforcement, focusing on crates thrown onto the Blue Stacking Pad.  I\'m ensuring they only fill slots relevant to the active `[Q]` build order pattern. I\'ve defined slot indices for the 2x2x2 pad and, based on the pattern, I am creating allowed slots, like single crate patterns `[0]` and all the way up to full cube crates `[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]`. In FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx I\'ll be rendering ghost wireframe slot boxes.\n\n\n**Visualizing UI Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on UI feedback for the Blue Stacking Pad. I\'ll highlight the slots matching the active `[Q]` pattern with cyan/lime translucent wireframes, including a bounding box mirroring the pattern\'s 3D dimensions. When allowed slots are filled, the AI Buddy will trigger crafting, or the hologram will flash. This aims to provide clear visual cues.\n\nI\'m also working on camera adjustments. I plan to zoom out the camera about 20% and implement scroll wheel zooming for a wider perspective, and adding a mini-radar to the playing HUD, so that the player is always aware of their surroundings.\n\n\n**Visualizing Kode Luau Terrain**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on rendering the Kode Luau world within the game. I\'m working on the arena\'s grassland and dirt crossroad layout, including the Blue and Red HQ squares. I\'m integrating crates, AI buddies, and the player, all with appropriate color coding. Moreover, I\'m integrating radarEntities into HudSnapshot so that the HUD\'s mini-radar is up-to-date with live world coordinates.\n\n**Defining AI Command Trigger**\n\nNow I am working on the command triggering, specifically via the `[V]` key. I\'m implementing a raycast from the player\'s mouse crosshair to check the 3D world position. The goal is that, if the cursor is near a crate, the AI command is set to \"HARVEST\", or if it\'s near an enemy, it\'s set to \"ATTACK\".\n\n\n**Implementing AI Command Logic**\n\nI\'m now expanding the AI command logic. I\'ve integrated `DEFEND` when the cursor is over Blue HQ or the Blue Stacking Pad. For unoccupied Blue Tanks, the `MOUNT_TANK` command will be assigned. I\'m also adding a cycle for open ground commands. Finally, pressing `[V]` will trigger all AI buddies to salute with an overhead badge, displaying the active order, and enabling AI buddies to mount and drive a tank.\n\n\n"
