  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Implementation Plan**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how the four game requirements will be implemented across `/src/game/FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx` and `/src/App.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m examining how `bluePadSlots` and `redPadSlots` are initialized as empty arrays for a clean match start. Next, I\'ll be reviewing how the state of these arrays is updated as pieces are played.\n\n\n**Reviewing Gameplay Initialization**\n\nI\'m now thinking about how the game begins. Specifically, I\'m verifying the initial state of the `tanks` array, ensuring it\'s empty at match start. Tanks will only spawn after crates are stacked, and the player crafts them, not before. I am also working on `BUILD_ORDER_CYCLE` and the Ghost Wireframe Outline.\n\n\n**Visualizing Ghost Wireframes**\n\nI\'m now implementing the ghost wireframes. I\'m focusing on the `ghostPatternBox` and the eight individual slot boxes (`ghostSlotMeshes`). I\'m using `BUILD_ORDER_SPECS` to position and scale the `ghostPatternBox` correctly. I\'m also ensuring the visibility of each `ghostSlotMeshes[i]` is correctly tied to the active build order and slot availability. I\'ll make sure the ghost visuals are crisp. I\'m making progress in getting the wireframe to represent which slots are available at any time. I am making it so that these only show the allowed slots, from the active `[Q]` build order.\n\n\n**Adjusting UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating UI updates. When no crates are present, the title and subtitle accurately reflect the active build order [Q]. Pressing [Q] to change build orders necessitates automatic crate rearrangement to align with the new pattern\'s allowed slots, ejecting any excess.\n\n\n\n**Refining Camera View**\n\nI\'ve just been implementing the camera zoom feature. I\'ve set the default zoom to 1.22, providing a wider field of view. I\'m also now adding mouse wheel scrolling to smoothly zoom the camera. I\'ve also incorporated the new `camOffset` to get the perfect tactical viewpoint. Finally, I\'ve started the mini radar feature. I\'m adding `radarDots: RadarDot[]` to `HudSnapshot` for the radar display.\n\n\n**Implementing Mini-Radar**\n\nI\'m now integrating the mini-radar UI element in `/src/App.tsx`. I\'m focusing on rendering a comic-style `w-24 h-24 sm:w-28 sm:h-28` radar within the top-right cluster, immediately adjacent to the existing `Kode Luau` button. The radar will feature a green meadow background with dirt paths and the Central Drop Zone ring. I\'m adding dots to the radar display to represent the real-time positions of various game elements: crates, AI buddies, player, tanks, and the HQ\'s / pads.\n\n\n"
