  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 2
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **Core Request**: Perfect the final 4 Team Buddies PS1 gameplay details in `/src/game/FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx`, `/src/App.tsx`, `/src/game/rules.ts`, and sync them with the Roblox Studio Luau scripts in `/src/data/buddyBlitzLuauSuite.ts`:\n     1. **Mulai dari Nol (Clean Match Start)**:\n        - At match start or reset, `Stacking Pad 2x2x2` starts completely empty (`0/8` crates) and **no free Tank** is pre-parked next to the base. Tanks ONLY spawn after the player or AI stacks 8 crates (`2x2x2`) on the Stacking Pad and presses `[F]`.\n     2. **Ghost Wireframe Outline pada Stacking Pad Sesuai Tombol `[Q]`**:\n        - Pressing `[Q]` cycles the build order across all 6 Team Buddies shapes (`1x1x1` Lite Weapon, `2x1x1` Grenade, `1x1x2` Buddy T1, `2x2x1` Heavy Weapon, `2x1x2` Buddy T2, `2x2x2` Lyo Tank).\n        - Displays a translucent **Ghost Wireframe Outline** (`ghostPatternBox` + `ghostSlotMeshes`) on the Blue Stacking Pad matching the active `[Q]` shape, and strictly constrains crates thrown by the player or AI to ONLY fill the slots belonging to that active `[Q]` pattern.\n     3. **Zoom-Out Sedikit Kamera & Tambahkan Mini-Radar Team Buddies**:\n        - Zoom out the camera by ~22% (`cameraZoom = 1.22` default + mouse scroll wheel zoom support `0.78..1.65`) so the player can see the Base HQ, Stacking Pad 2x2x2, and the road toward the Drop Zone simultaneously.\n        - Add a real-time **Mini-Radar** in the top-right corner of the HUD (to the left of the `Kode Luau` button) displaying the positions of the player, Allied AI Buddies, Red Enemies, falling/grounded Crates (Red & Blue Super), Tanks, and both Base HQs.\n     4. **Teropong Perintah AI (`[V]`) Berdasarkan Target Kursor + AI Salute**:\n        - Allow pressing `[V]` while aiming the mouse crosshair at a 3D target to issue context-sensitive AI Squad orders (aim at Crate -> `HARVEST`, aim at Enemy/Red HQ -> `ATTACK`, aim at Blue HQ/Pad -> `DEFEND`, aim at empty Tank -> `MOUNT`, or cycle modes on open ground).\n        - When `[V]` is pressed, all living allied AI Buddies perform a **Salute animation** (raising right hand to forehead) with an overhead 3D Salute Badge (`HORMAT!`) above their head.\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Completed Earlier & Verified**:\n     - The core 5 Team Buddies x Lyo 3D gameplay overhaul (`FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx`, `App.tsx`, `rules.ts`, `rules.test.ts`, `buddyBlitzLuauSuite.ts`) was compiled, tested (8/8 unit tests passing), and verified in Playwright with 0 console errors.\n   - **Completed Code Edits in This Turn (Pending Final Test/Compile/Browser Verification)**:\n     - `/src/game/rules.ts`:\n       - Updated `BuildOrderTarget` to include all 6 shapes (`\'1x1x1\' | \'2x1x1\' | \'1x1x2\' | \'2x2x1\' | \'2x1x2\' | \'2x2x2\' | \'AUTO\'`).\n       - Added `BUILD_ORDER_SPECS` (defining `allowedSlots`, `targetCrates`, `ghostBoxSize`, and `ghostBoxCenter` for each shape) and `getBuildOrderAllowedSlots(buildOrder)`.\n       - Updated `chooseNextPadSlotIndex(slots, buildOrder)` to strictly fill only `allowedSlots` of the active pattern and return `-1` when that pattern is full.\n       - Added pure helper `resolveCursorCommandTarget(input)` to map cursor world coordinates `(cursorX, cursorZ)` onto `\'MOUNT\'`, `\'HARVEST\'`, `\'ATTACK\'`, `\'DEFEND\'`, or cycle fallback.\n     - `/src/game/rules.test.ts`:\n       - Updated test #8 (`chooseNextPadSlotIndex strictly enforces [Q] build order slots and stops when pattern is full`) and added test #9 (`resolveCursorCommandTarget maps cursor crosshair onto Crate, Enemy, Base, or Tank orders`).\n     - `/src/game/FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx`:\n       - **Clean Match Start**: `bluePadSlots` and `redPadSlots` initialize to 8 `\'empty\'` slots (`0/8`), and `tanks` initializes empty (`[]` \342\200\224 no free pre-parked tank).\n       - **Ghost Wireframe Outline (`[Q]`)**: Added `ghostPatternBox` (cyan outer wireframe bounding box) and 8 `ghostSlotMeshes` (lime wireframe slot cubes) on the Stacking Pad that update dynamically when `[Q]` is pressed and repack any existing pad crates into the new pattern\'s allowed slots.\n       - **Camera Zoom-Out (~22%) + Scroll Wheel Zoom**: Set default `cameraZoom = 1.22` and added `wheel` event listener to zoom smoothly between `0.78` and `1.65`.\n       - **Mini-Radar Data (`radarDots`)**: Populated `radarDots` in `HudSnapshot` every HUD tick with live world `(x, z)` positions of crates, tanks, allies, enemies, and player.\n       - **Cursor-Targeted AI Command (`[V]`) + Salute Animation**: Pressing `KeyV` resolves the command from `aimWorldPoint` via `resolveCursorCommandTarget`, triggers `triggerAlliedSalute` (`saluteTimer = 1.65s`, right arm raised to forehead + 3D `saluteSign` billboard above each allied AI Buddy), and supports AI Buddies mounting and driving crafted Blue Tanks (`occupiedByAiId`).\n     - `/src/App.tsx`:\n       - Updated `INITIAL_HUD` for Clean Match Start (`0/8` empty pad slots, `buildOrder: \'1x1x2\'`).\n       - Added dashed cyan Ghost slot indicators in the top-left Pad status bar for allowed slots in `getBuildOrderAllowedSlots(hud.buildOrder)`.\n       - Added the **Team Buddies Tactical Mini-Radar** (`aria-label=\"Mini Radar Arena\"`) in the top-right cluster (to the left of the `Kode Luau` button) rendering the crossroad paths, Central Drop Zone ring, Red HQ, Blue HQ, and live `hud.radarDots`.\n     - `/src/data/buddyBlitzLuauSuite.ts`:\n       - Synced all 4 features into the Roblox Studio Luau scripts (`CAM_DISTANCE = 42` + MouseWheel zoom, `CrateRecipes.BuildOrders` + `SelectionBox` Ghost Wireframe, `SpawnCraftedTank` BindableEvent with no free pre-spawned tanks, and `IssueCommandRemote` cursor-target resolution + `showSaluteBadge`).\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - `DISABLE_HMR=true` is active in this environment; after running `compile_applet`, `restart_dev_server` must be called before opening `http://localhost:3000` in `playwright-cli`.\n   - When `[Q]` is cycled while crates are already on the Blue Stacking Pad, repacking existing crates into `chooseNextPadSlotIndex(bluePadSlots, buildOrder)` (and ejecting any excess crates beside the pad) guarantees crates never occupy disallowed slots.\n\n4. **Errors & Fixes**\n   - **Resolved Earlier**: `TypeError: soundEngine.playPowerCore is not a function` \342\200\224 fixed by adding `playPowerCore()` to `SoundEngine` in `/src/game/audio.ts`.\n   - No new errors encountered.\n\n5. **Active Context**\n   - All code changes for the 4 new Team Buddies PS1 gameplay refinements have been written to `/src/game/rules.ts`, `/src/game/rules.test.ts`, `/src/game/FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx`, `/src/App.tsx`, and `/src/data/buddyBlitzLuauSuite.ts`.\n   - Verification (running unit tests, compiling, restarting dev server, and inspecting live screenshots in Playwright) is the immediate next step.\n\n6. **Next Steps**\n   1. Run the unit test suite (`npx --yes tsx --test src/game/rules.test.ts`) and `compile_applet` to verify all 9 unit tests pass and TypeScript compiles with 0 errors.\n   2. Call `restart_dev_server` so port 3000 serves the updated build.\n   3. Run a `playwright-cli` verification session (`trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT`) at `http://localhost:3000?autostart=1`:\n      - Verify Clean Match Start (`0/8` empty pad with `1x1x2` Ghost Wireframe Outline visible, no free tank parked, zoomed-out camera showing Base HQ + Stacking Pad + Drop Zone road, and Mini-Radar in the top-right) and capture `r6-clean-start-radar.png`.\n      - Press `q` to cycle the Ghost Wireframe pattern (`2x2x1` / `2x1x2` / `2x2x2`) and press `v` to trigger the AI Salute (`HORMAT!`) and capture `r6-ghost-and-salute.png`.\n      - Check `playwright-cli console error` to confirm 0 errors.\n      - Inspect both screenshots with `view_file` (`AbsolutePath: \"/r6-clean-start-radar.png\"` and `\"/r6-ghost-and-salute.png\"`), then clean up temporary files (`rm -rf r6-*.png .playwright-cli`).\n   4. Provide a concise summary of the 4 completed gameplay refinements to the user.\n\n7. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Follow `ultra-mode` verification discipline: run unit tests, `compile_applet`, `restart_dev_server`, and inspect real browser screenshots via `view_file` before finishing.\n   - Maintain clean, concise UI text with no emojis or unrequested icons.\n</summary>"
