  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Asset Loading**\n\nI\'m currently focused on asset loading strategies. My latest thought involves replacing the current procedural generation of game elements like trees, tanks, props, grass, and lighting within `/src/game/FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx`. The goal is to utilize real `.glb` models loaded through `GLTFLoader` and `DRACOLoader` instead.\n\n\n**Implementing Asset Loading**\n\nI\'m now diving into specific asset loading, starting with trees. I plan to load `tree-1a.glb` and `tree-1b.glb`, using their trunk meshes and the existing `TreeLeaves` shader with precise parameters for leaf cards, colors, and wind effects. Next, I\'ll tackle tanks, loading `player.glb`, `fodder.glb`, and `boss.glb` to build crafted tanks with their components like body, turret, and track instances.\n\n\n**Expanding Asset Implementation**\n\nI\'m now expanding asset implementation to include Lyo Tank features, like an optional toggle for a showcase with the exact inverted-hull black stroke outline and toon shader. I also plan to load specific factory props like hydrants, explosive barrels, and various boxes. The decompiled Lyo InfiniteGrass shader will replace my existing simple grass, ensuring precise blade geometry and color matching for the visual fidelity of the grass.\n\n\n"
