    thinking: "**Importing Essential Components**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial components into `/src/game/FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx`. This involves importing `loadAllRealLyoAssets`, various creation functions such as `createLyoInfiniteGrassSystem`, and population functions for trees and tanks. I am also importing spawning functions for props and retrieving the default light direction, along with necessary asset types and wind uniforms. This is the first step!\n\n\n**Implementing Real Assets**\n\nI\'ve replaced the old ConeGeometry grass with `createLyoInfiniteGrassSystem`, our decompiled Lyo shader with specific blade configuration and wind effects. I\'m also loading real .glb models, including player, boss, and fodder, along with trees and props. I\'ve focused on replacing the existing trees with the real `tree-1b.glb` and `tree-1a.glb` models and implementing associated foliage. I am now working on tank replacements.\n\n\n**Adding Real Tanks**\n\nI am now integrating the real `player.glb` tank, along with its 14-segment `player-track.json` tracks. I\'m focusing on mirrored wheels and covers via `populateRealLyoTankFromGlb`. I\'m also placing a showcase tank on the Factory Playground perimeter. I\'m remembering the criteria: tanks should only appear after players stack 8 crates and press [F], or trigger the test, while also placing power cores, turbines, hydrants, and barrels. Now, crafted tanks will use the real `player.glb` and `player-track.json`.\n\n\n"
