  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visual Discoveries**\n\nI\'m finding the visual inspection incredibly valuable, especially after reviewing `r7-real-glb-lyo-clean.png` and `r7-real-glb-lyo-tank.png` alongside the console logs. My focus now is dissecting the discoveries from the image, starting with observations from the `r7-real-glb-lyo-tank.png` file.\n\n\n**Correcting Code Referencing**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed a crucial bug: I was getting a `ReferenceError` because I was using the wrong variable name, `tankVehicles` instead of `tanks` within `FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx`. But the visual observations are more compelling. The textures on the road assets are great! I\'m now looking at the scale of `turbine.glb` and the odd tree setup. It seems `tree-1b.glb` contains every tree instance, not just a model.\n\n\n**Isolating Cloning Issues**\n\nI\'ve got it! The `template.scene.traverse(...)` function in `populateRealLyoTreeFromGlb` was the culprit. It was cloning every mesh within `tree-1b.glb`, not just the reference trees. The mini trunks scattered around were a dead giveaway. Now I\'m focused on the canopy issue, that\'s it! It seems to be related to the local offset or scale of `Tree_1B.REF`, or potentially the positioning of its `Tree_Foliage` nodes within `Tree_1B.REF`.\nI also need to check the grass blade system.\n\n\n"
