  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Leaf Clusters**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the visual characteristics of the `tree-1b.glb` purple tree and the `tree-1a.glb` golden tree. I\'m noting the subtle color variations, specifically the use of the hex codes like `#5e57a5` and `#eab308`. It appears the `TreeLeaves` are comprised of `80 planesPerCluster` and I am examining the overall aesthetic effect.\n\n\n**Analyzing Material Assignments**\n\nI\'m now investigating the interplay between `InfiniteGrass`, `InfiniteGrassPetals`, and roadside objects like the `hydrant.glb` and `explosive-barrel.glb`. I\'m fascinated by the interplay of `halftone shading` and `comic stroke trunk`, and I\'m interested in the interplay of green hues (`#1b6e1e`, `#75d424`, `#d1f542`) and yellow/purple petals (`#fff04a`, `#b366ff`). I\'ve encountered a critical error in `Mesh.clone()` that failed due to `ShaderMaterial.toJSON`.\n\n\n**Debugging Shader Serialization**\n\nI\'m now focused on a serialization error related to `ShaderMaterial` within the Three.js `clone()` function. It seems `ShaderMaterial.toJSON()` is causing a stack overflow when dealing with `KTX2` textures during the cloning of objects, specifically when `userData` contains a `ShaderMaterial`. I\'m also puzzled by the appearance of a tan cylinder (`turbine.glb`) on the screen\'s left edge, which I\'m tracing back to the way multiple `WindTurbine` instances are handled during the loading and spawning process. It appears `spawnRealLyoPropFromGlb` is picking up every instance in the original `glb` file.\n\n\n**Investigating Node Hierarchy**\n\nI\'m now tracing why the `WindTurbine` model ended up near the camera. It turns out the GLTF loader creates a `THREE.Group` named `WindTurbine.REF` when a node has both a mesh and children, like `turbine.glb`. Specifically, the loader puts the mesh as a child. I\'m focusing on the coordinates in `FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx` to understand the placement of the turbine, which led to it appearing on the left edge of the screen. I see it was placed near the camera\'s near-plane.\n\n\n**Repositioning Scene Elements**\n\nI\'m now implementing the repositioning of several key assets. I\'ve adjusted the coordinates for `turbine.glb` and `power-core.glb` to eliminate camera clipping, aiming for a more visible and aesthetically pleasing placement within the arena. I\'m also addressing the incorrect mesh placement. I\'ve identified problematic code in `/src/game/lyoAssetsAndShaders.ts` which needs to be updated. I also aim to clone `glbBarrel` and `glbTurret` before calling the upgrade. I aim to ensure a cleaner material upgrade.\n\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_233850"
      name: "multi_replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"Description\":\"Remove ShaderMaterial from mesh.userData and clone glbTurret/glbBarrel before applying ShaderMaterial in populateRealLyoTankFromGlb\", \"Instruction\":\"Update upgradeMeshToLyoWorldMaterial and populateRealLyoTankFromGlb in /src/game/lyoAssetsAndShaders.ts\", \"ReplacementChunks\":[{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":248, \"ReplacementContent\":\"  mesh.material = mat;\\n}\", \"StartLine\":244, \"TargetContent\":\"  mesh.material = mat;\\n  mesh.userData.baseMaterial = mat;\\n}\"}, {\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":1199, \"ReplacementContent\":\"  const tint = isSuper ? \'#00d2ff\' : undefined;\\n  const tankScale = 1.15;\\n\\n  // 1. Reparent Player_Turret and Player_Barrel into turretGroup and barrelGroup BEFORE upgrading materials\\n  // so Object3D.clone() never serializes ShaderMaterial uniforms via JSON.stringify(userData)\\n  if (glbBarrel) {\\n    const barrelMesh = glbBarrel.clone(false);\\n    barrelMesh.position.set(0, 0, 0);\\n    barrelMesh.rotation.set(0, 0, 0);\\n    barrelMesh.scale.setScalar(tankScale);\\n    barrelGroup.add(barrelMesh);\\n    glbBarrel.visible = false;\\n  }\\n\\n  if (glbTurret) {\\n    const turretMesh = glbTurret.clone(false);\\n    turretMesh.position.set(0, 0.15, 0);\\n    turretMesh.rotation.set(0, 0, 0);\\n    turretMesh.scale.setScalar(tankScale);\\n    turretGroup.add(turretMesh);\\n    glbTurret.visible = false;\\n  }\\n\\n  // 2. Mirror Left_Wheel_01..04 and TrackCover_Left_01..03 onto the right side (exact B1Nq4Kq6.js logic)\\n  const leftWheels = findPrefixList(\'Left_Wheel\');\\n  leftWheels.forEach((wheel, idx) => {\\n    wheel.updateMatrix();\\n    const mirroredGeo = createMirroredGeometry(wheel.geometry);\\n    const rightWheel = new THREE.Mesh(mirroredGeo, wheel.material);\\n    rightWheel.name = `Right_Wheel_0${idx + 1}`;\\n    rightWheel.position.copy(wheel.position);\\n    rightWheel.position.z = 2 * bodyCenterZ - wheel.position.z;\\n    rightWheel.quaternion.copy(wheel.quaternion);\\n    rightWheel.scale.copy(wheel.scale);\\n    (wheel.parent || clonedRoot).add(rightWheel);\\n  });\\n\\n  const leftCovers = findPrefixList(\'TrackCover_Left\');\\n  leftCovers.forEach((cover, idx) => {\\n    cover.updateMatrix();\\n    const mirroredGeo = createMirroredGeometry(cover.geometry);\\n    const rightCover = new THREE.Mesh(mirroredGeo, cover.material);\\n    rightCover.name = `TrackCover_Right_0${idx + 1}`;\\n    rightCover.position.copy(cover.position);\\n    rightCover.position.z = -cover.position.z;\\n    rightCover.quaternion.copy(cover.quaternion);\\n    rightCover.scale.copy(cover.scale);\\n    (cover.parent || clonedRoot).add(rightCover);\\n  });\\n\\n  // 3. Upgrade all visual meshes in clonedRoot, turretGroup, and barrelGroup with Lyo\'s WorldMaterial + Stroke Outline\\n  const upgradeHierarchy = (rootObj: THREE.Object3D) => {\\n    rootObj.traverse((obj) => {\\n      if ((obj as THREE.Mesh).isMesh) {\\n        const m = obj as THREE.Mesh;\\n        if (m.userData.isModelStroke || m === muzzleFlash) return;\\n        if (isLyoColliderOrHelperNode(m)) {\\n          m.visible = false;\\n          return;\\n        }\\n        m.castShadow = !isSoftwareGl;\\n        m.receiveShadow = !isSoftwareGl;\\n        upgradeMeshToLyoWorldMaterial(m, windUniforms, tint);\\n        const stroke = createLyoStrokeMesh(m.geometry, 0.026);\\n        if (stroke) m.add(stroke);\\n      }\\n    });\\n  };\\n  upgradeHierarchy(clonedRoot);\\n  upgradeHierarchy(turretGroup);\\n  upgradeHierarchy(barrelGroup);\\n\\n  // 4. Instance Player_Track along player-track.json CatmullRomCurve3 (14 segments per side)\\n  if (glbTrackSeg && glbTrackSeg.geometry && trackPoints && trackPoints.length > 4) {\\n    glbTrackSeg.visible = false;\\n    const uniquePts = trackPoints.filter((pt, i) => {\\n      if (i === 0) return true;\\n      const prev = trackPoints[i - 1];\\n      return !(pt.x === prev.x && pt.y === prev.y && pt.z === prev.z);\\n    });\\n    const leftPts = uniquePts.map((p) => new THREE.Vector3(p.x, p.y, p.z - 0.02));\\n    const rightPts = uniquePts.map((p) => new THREE.Vector3(p.x, p.y, 2 * bodyCenterZ - p.z - 0.02));\\n    const leftCurve = new THREE.CatmullRomCurve3(leftPts, true, \'centripetal\');\\n    const rightCurve = new THREE.CatmullRomCurve3(rightPts, true, \'centripetal\');\\n    const numSegments = 14;\\n\\n    const buildTrackBelt = (curve: THREE.CatmullRomCurve3, isRight: boolean) => {\\n      const geo = isRight ? createMirroredGeometry(glbTrackSeg.geometry) : glbTrackSeg.geometry.clone();\\n      const inst = new THREE.InstancedMesh(geo, glbTrackSeg.material, numSegments);\\n      const dummy = new THREE.Object3D();\\n      const frames = curve.computeFrenetFrames(numSegments, true);\\n      for (let i = 0; i < numSegments; i++) {\\n        const pt = curve.getPointAt(i / numSegments);\\n        dummy.position.copy(pt);\\n        const tangent = frames.tangents[i];\\n        const normal = frames.normals[i];\\n        const binormal = frames.binormals[i];\\n        const m = new THREE.Matrix4().makeBasis(tangent, normal, binormal);\\n        dummy.quaternion.setFromRotationMatrix(m);\\n        dummy.rotateX(-Math.PI / 2);\\n        dummy.rotateY(Math.PI);\\n        dummy.updateMatrix();\\n        inst.setMatrixAt(i, dummy.matrix);\\n      }\\n      inst.instanceMatrix.needsUpdate = true;\\n      clonedRoot.add(inst);\\n    };\\n\\n    buildTrackBelt(leftCurve, false);\\n    buildTrackBelt(rightCurve, true);\\n  }\\n\\n  clonedRoot.scale.setScalar(tankScale);\\n\\n  // Align chassis to ground (y = 0)\\n  const hullBox = new THREE.Box3().setFromObject(clonedRoot);\\n  clonedRoot.position.y = -hullBox.min.y;\\n  bodyGroup.add(clonedRoot);\\n}\", \"StartLine\":1084, \"TargetContent\":\"  const tint = isSuper ? \'#00d2ff\' : undefined;\\n\\n  // Upgrade all visual meshes in clonedRoot with Lyo\'s WorldMaterial + Stroke Outline\\n  clonedRoot.traverse((obj) => {\\n    if ((obj as THREE.Mesh).isMesh) {\\n      const m = obj as THREE.Mesh;\\n      if (isLyoColliderOrHelperNode(m)) {\\n        m.visible = false;\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      m.castShadow = !isSoftwareGl;\\n      m.receiveShadow = !isSoftwareGl;\\n      upgradeMeshToLyoWorldMaterial(m, windUniforms, tint);\\n      const stroke = createLyoStrokeMesh(m.geometry, 0.026);\\n      if (stroke) m.add(stroke);\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  // Mirror Left_Wheel_01..04 and TrackCover_Left_01..03 onto the right side (exact B1Nq4Kq6.js logic)\\n  const leftWheels = findPrefixList(\'Left_Wheel\');\\n  leftWheels.forEach((wheel, idx) => {\\n    wheel.updateMatrix();\\n    const mirroredGeo = createMirroredGeometry(wheel.geometry);\\n    const rightWheel = new THREE.Mesh(mirroredGeo, wheel.material);\\n    rightWheel.name = `Right_Wheel_0${idx + 1}`;\\n    rightWheel.position.copy(wheel.position);\\n    rightWheel.position.z = 2 * bodyCenterZ - wheel.position.z;\\n    rightWheel.quaternion.copy(wheel.quaternion);\\n    rightWheel.scale.copy(wheel.scale);\\n    const stroke = createLyoStrokeMesh(mirroredGeo, 0.024);\\n    if (stroke) rightWheel.add(stroke);\\n    (wheel.parent || clonedRoot).add(rightWheel);\\n  });\\n\\n  const leftCovers = findPrefixList(\'TrackCover_Left\');\\n  leftCovers.forEach((cover, idx) => {\\n    cover.updateMatrix();\\n    const mirroredGeo = createMirroredGeometry(cover.geometry);\\n    const rightCover = new THREE.Mesh(mirroredGeo, cover.material);\\n    rightCover.name = `TrackCover_Right_0${idx + 1}`;\\n    rightCover.position.copy(cover.position);\\n    rightCover.position.z = -cover.position.z;\\n    rightCover.quaternion.copy(cover.quaternion);\\n    rightCover.scale.copy(cover.scale);\\n    const stroke = createLyoStrokeMesh(mirroredGeo, 0.024);\\n    if (stroke) rightCover.add(stroke);\\n    (cover.parent || clonedRoot).add(rightCover);\\n  });\\n\\n  // Instance Player_Track along player-track.json CatmullRomCurve3 (14 segments per side)\\n  if (glbTrackSeg && glbTrackSeg.geometry && trackPoints && trackPoints.length > 4) {\\n    glbTrackSeg.visible = false;\\n    const uniquePts = trackPoints.filter((pt, i) => {\\n      if (i === 0) return true;\\n      const prev = trackPoints[i - 1];\\n      return !(pt.x === prev.x && pt.y === prev.y && pt.z === prev.z);\\n    });\\n    const leftPts = uniquePts.map((p) => new THREE.Vector3(p.x, p.y, p.z - 0.02));\\n    const rightPts = uniquePts.map((p) => new THREE.Vector3(p.x, p.y, 2 * bodyCenterZ - p.z - 0.02));\\n    const leftCurve = new THREE.CatmullRomCurve3(leftPts, true, \'centripetal\');\\n    const rightCurve = new THREE.CatmullRomCurve3(rightPts, true, \'centripetal\');\\n    const numSegments = 14;\\n\\n    const buildTrackBelt = (curve: THREE.CatmullRomCurve3, isRight: boolean) => {\\n      const geo = isRight ? createMirroredGeometry(glbTrackSeg.geometry) : glbTrackSeg.geometry.clone();\\n      const inst = new THREE.InstancedMesh(geo, glbTrackSeg.material, numSegments);\\n      const dummy = new THREE.Object3D();\\n      const frames = curve.computeFrenetFrames(numSegments, true);\\n      for (let i = 0; i < numSegments; i++) {\\n        const pt = curve.getPointAt(i / numSegments);\\n        dummy.position.copy(pt);\\n        const tangent = frames.tangents[i];\\n        const normal = frames.normals[i];\\n        const binormal = frames.binormals[i];\\n        const m = new THREE.Matrix4().makeBasis(tangent, normal, binormal);\\n        dummy.quaternion.setFromRotationMatrix(m);\\n        dummy.rotateX(-Math.PI / 2);\\n        dummy.rotateY(Math.PI);\\n        dummy.updateMatrix();\\n        inst.setMatrixAt(i, dummy.matrix);\\n      }\\n      inst.instanceMatrix.needsUpdate = true;\\n      clonedRoot.add(inst);\\n    };\\n\\n    buildTrackBelt(leftCurve, false);\\n    buildTrackBelt(rightCurve, true);\\n  }\\n\\n  // Reparent Player_Turret and Player_Barrel into our interactive turretGroup and barrelGroup\\n  // so 360\302\260 mouse aiming and cannon recoil work seamlessl