  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 4
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **Current User Request:** Overhaul the game mode controls in `src/game/FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx`, `src/game/lyoAssetsAndShaders.ts`, and `src/App.tsx` into **3 Separate Modes** switchable at any time via a **Toggle Switch in the Top Bar**:\n     1. **Mode 1 (Default on open): `SANDBOX TEST (NO NPC)`**\n        - **Disable/Remove All NPCs & AI:** Do NOT spawn Red enemies and do NOT move Allied Blue AI Buddies automatically. Bases must never be attacked on their own in this mode.\n        - **Focus on Player Mechanics Testing:** Player runs freely as a Buddy (`WASD`), picks up/throws Red & Blue Super Crates (`[E]`), stacks them on the `Stacking Pad 2x2x2`, presses `[F]` to craft Weapons or the real `player.glb` Lyo Tank, and mounts/dismounts the Tank (`[G]`) without enemy interference.\n        - **Quick Sandbox Action Buttons in UI:**\n          - `+ Drop Peti Merah`\n          - `+ Drop Peti Biru`\n          - `+ Spawn Lyo Tank di Depanku`\n     2. **Mode 2: `MAP EDITOR` (For Building & Arranging the Arena)**\n        - **Editor Camera (Top-Down / Wide Orbit Zoom):** Raise the camera high so the entire map (Blue HQ, Red HQ, Dirt Roads, Drop Zones, and Trees) is clearly visible in one screen. Allow camera panning via middle/right-click drag or `WASD`, and zoom in/out with the mouse scroll wheel.\n        - **Lyo `.glb` Asset Placement Toolbar:** Side palette of objects to click-to-place onto the ground at the cursor point, right-click to delete, `R` to rotate, `[` and `]` to scale:\n          1. `Pohon Ungu Lyo` (`tree-1b.glb` + lush purple `TreeLeaves` foliage)\n          2. `Pohon Emas Lyo` (`tree-1a.glb` + lush yellow/gold `TreeLeaves` foliage)\n          3. `Kincir Angin` (`turbine.glb`)\n          4. `Power Core` (`power-core.glb`)\n          5. `Barikade / Pagar Beton` (`concrete-fence-1a.glb` & `barricade-1a.glb`)\n          6. `Tong Peledak & Hidran` (`explosive-barrel.glb` & `hydrant.glb`)\n          7. `Pindah Posisi Blue HQ / Red HQ / Stacking Pad / Crate Drop Zone` (reposition core arena structures by clicking on the ground)\n        - **Fix Tree Scale on Map:** Ensure all default trees (`tree-1b.glb` and `tree-1a.glb`) have a proportional height of **~8\342\200\22310 units** (much taller than the Buddy character) with lush purple/gold leaf canopies on their branches, and place several default trees near the player\'s starting area (`z \342\211\210 +10..+16`) so they are immediately visible!\n        - **Map Persistence Buttons:**\n          - `Simpan Layout Map` (save to `localStorage` & allow exporting JSON / Luau table)\n          - `Reset Map Default`\n     3. **Mode 3: `RUN MATCH (WITH AI)`**\n        - Red Enemy NPCs and Allied Blue AI Buddies **ONLY** spawn and move when the player explicitly clicks `RUN MATCH (WITH AI)`.\n        - Switching back to `SANDBOX TEST` or `MAP EDITOR` immediately clears all AI NPCs and stops all attacks.\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Completed & Verified in Prior Turns:**\n     - Captured all 48 `.glb` models, 4 `.json` track files, 21 `.ktx2` textures, 1 `.bin`, and 18 `.webp` files from `https://longhoang-lyo.com/` after clicking `\"LET\'S GO\"`. Saved in `/extracted_lyo_assets/` and mirrored in `/public/extracted_lyo_assets/`, with `/public/draco/` and `/public/basis/` decoders configured.\n     - Wrote `/LYO_TECHNICAL_EXTRACTION.md` with decompiled TSL/GLSL shaders (`InfiniteGrass`, `InfiniteGrassPetals`, `TreeLeaves`, `WorldMaterial`, `StrokeMaterial`) and `player.glb` + `player-track.json` assembly.\n     - Created `/src/game/lyoAssetsAndShaders.ts` and integrated real `.glb` loading (`player.glb`, `tree-1b.glb`, `tree-1a.glb`, `power-core.glb`, `turbine.glb`, `hydrant.glb`, `explosive-barrel.glb`) into `/src/game/FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx`.\n     - Verified build (`compile_applet`), unit tests (`npx --yes tsx --test src/game/rules.test.ts`), and Playwright rendering with 0 console errors.\n   - **In Progress (Just Started for Current User Request):**\n     - Read `/src/App.tsx` (lines 1\342\200\223500) and `/src/game/FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx` (lines 1\342\200\223150) to prepare the 3-mode architecture (`sandbox` | `editor` | `match`). No files have been modified yet for this new turn.\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - **Available `.glb` Models in `/public/extracted_lyo_assets/models/`:**\n     - `tree-1b.glb` (has `Tree_1B.REF` + `Tree_Foliage.001..009`), `tree-1a.glb` (has `Tree_1A.REF` + `Tree_Foliage.010..017`)\n     - `turbine.glb` (`WindTurbine.REF`), `power-core.glb` (`PowerCore.001`), `hydrant.glb` (`Hydrant.REF`), `explosive-barrel.glb` (`ExplosiveBarrel.REF`)\n     - `concrete-fence-1a.glb`, `barricade-1a.glb` (already downloaded in `/public/extracted_lyo_assets/models/`! Need to add `concreteFenceGltf` and `barricadeGltf` to `loadAllRealLyoAssets` in `/src/game/lyoAssetsAndShaders.ts`).\n   - **Tree Scaling (`populateRealLyoTreeFromGlb` in `/src/game/lyoAssetsAndShaders.ts`):**\n     - Currently `refScale` in `populateRealLyoTreeFromGlb` uses `sourceRoot.scale.x` (`0.4362676`), which makes the trunk ~4.3m tall. To make trees **8\342\200\22310 units tall** as requested (`sekitar 8\342\200\22310 unit, jauh lebih tinggi dari karakter Buddy`) with lush canopies, we should support a `userScale` multiplier (defaulting to ~`1.95`\303\227 on top of `0.4362676` so total tree height is ~8.8\342\200\2239.5 units, and scaling `uLeafScale` / cluster scale proportionally so the canopy is super lush and sits right on the branches).\n\n4. **Errors & Fixes**\n   - **Previous `ShaderMaterial.toJSON` RangeError during `Mesh.clone()`:** Caused by storing `THREE.ShaderMaterial` inside `mesh.userData.baseMaterial` and calling `.clone()`. Fixed in `/src/game/lyoAssetsAndShaders.ts` by never storing `ShaderMaterial` in `userData` and cloning `glbTurret`/`glbBarrel` before upgrading materials. Keep this pattern when cloning editor props!\n   - **Key `KeyR` collision in `src/App.tsx`:** Notice in `src/App.tsx` line 188, pressing `KeyR` currently opens `isReaModalOpen` (`Kode Luau` modal). In `MAP EDITOR` mode (and generally), `R` is requested to rotate the selected/hovered editor object (`R untuk putar`), so we must disable the `KeyR -> setIsReaModalOpen(true)` shortcut in `src/App.tsx` so `R` rotates objects in `MAP EDITOR` cleanly without popping up the modal!\n\n5. **Active Context**\n   - Dev server is running on port 3000.\n   - All skills (`ultra-mode`, `computer-use`, `threejs`, `frontend-design`) have been read.\n\n6. **Next Steps**\n   1. **Update `/src/game/lyoAssetsAndShaders.ts`:**\n      - Add `concreteFenceGltf` (`/extracted_lyo_assets/models/concrete-fence-1a.glb`) and `barricadeGltf` (`/extracted_lyo_assets/models/barricade-1a.glb`) to `LoadedLyoAssets` and `loadAllRealLyoAssets()`.\n      - Update `populateRealLyoTreeFromGlb` to accept a `heightScale = 1.95` parameter so default trees are **8.5\342\200\2239.5 units tall** (much taller than the Buddy character) with lush, dense purple/gold `TreeLeaves` canopies (`uLeafScale = 2.4 * heightScale` or scaled via `trunkGroup.scale.setScalar(heightScale)` so both trunk and `foliageInstanced` scale together seamlessly!).\n   2. **Update `/src/game/FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx`:**\n      - Add `playMode: \'sandbox\' | \'editor\' | \'match\'` prop (default `\'sandbox\'`), plus editor state/callbacks or custom event listeners (`lyo-sandbox-action`, `lyo-editor-action`).\n      - **Mode 1 (`sandbox` - Default):**\n        - Spawn ONLY the Player Buddy (`playerUnit`). Do NOT spawn Red enemy buddies and do NOT spawn AI Blue buddies (or clear all non-player `buddyUnits` when switching to `\'sandbox\'` or `\'editor\'`).\n        - Disable automatic enemy/ally AI movement and base attacks when `playMode !== \'match\'`.\n        - Handle Sandbox quick actions:\n          - `drop-red-crate`: spawns a Red Crate right in front of the player (`playerUnit.x \302\261 ...`, grounded or low drop so it\'s immediately usable).\n          - `drop-super-crate`: spawns a Blue Super Crate right in front of the player.\n          - `spawn-tank`: spawns a real `player.glb` Blue Lyo Tank 3.5m in front of the player.\n      - **Mode 2 (`editor` - Map Editor):**\n        - Switch camera to a high top-down / wide-angle overview (`y \342\211\210 42`, looking at `(camPanX, 0, camPanZ)`) where Blue HQ, Red HQ, Dirt Roads, Drop Zones, and all Trees are visible at once.\n        - Allow panning with `WASD` or right/middle mouse drag, and zooming with mouse wheel (`cameraZoom` range `0.55` to `2.4`).\n        - Support placing & editing map items stored in a serializable `MapLayoutData` structure (persisted to `localStorage` under `\'lyo_custom_map_layout_v1\'`):\n          - Placed objects list (`id`, `kind`: `\'tree_purple\' | \'tree_gold\' | \'turbine\' | \'power_core\' | \'concrete_fence\' | \'barricade\' | \'explosive_barrel\' | \'hydrant\'`, `x`, `z`, `rotY`, `scale`).\n          - Core structure positions (`blueHq: {x, z}`, `redHq: {x, z}`, `bluePad: {x, z}`, `redPad: {x, z}`, `centerDropZone: {x, z}`).\n          - In `editor` mode:\n            - Show a 3D placement cursor ring/ghost on the ground at `aimWorldPoint`.\n            - Left-click on ground places the active tool item (or moves the selected structure if tool #7 is active).\n            - Right-click on/near an existing placed object deletes it.\n            - Pressing `R` rotates the active placement angle (and nearest/last placed object) by 45\302\260 (`Math.PI / 4`).\n            - Pressing `[` and `]` adjusts the scale (`0.5x` to `2.5x`) of the active placement / nearest object.\n            - Buttons for `Simpan Layout Map` (saves to `localStorage` and copies/shows JSON + Luau table export toast/modal) and `Reset Map Default`.\n        - Ensure default map layout places 8\342\200\22310 unit tall `tree-1b.glb` (purple) and `tree-1a.glb` (gold) trees including several near the player start (`(-7.5, 11.5)`, `(7.5, 11.5)`, `(-11.5, 15.5)`, `(11.5, 15.5)`) so they are immediately visible on screen.\n      - **Mode 3 (`match` - Run Match With AI):**\n        - When switching to `\'match\'`, spawn the Allied Blue AI Buddy and 3 Red Enemy AI Buddies and enable full AI harvesting, crafting, and combat.\n        - When switching away from `\'match\'` to `\'sandbox\'` or `\'editor\'`, immediately remove all non-player `buddyUnits`, clear active projectiles, and stop base attacks.\n   3. **Update `/src/App.tsx`:**\n      - Add the prominent **3-Mode Toggle Switch Bar** at the top center of the screen (`SANDBOX TEST (NO NPC)` | `MAP EDITOR` | `RUN MATCH (WITH AI)`).\n      - When `playMode === \'sandbox\'`, render the Sandbox Quick Test Toolbar (`+ Drop Peti Merah`, `+ Drop Peti Biru`, `+ Spawn Lyo Tank di Depanku`).\n      - When `playMode === \'editor\'`, render the Map Editor Side Palette (the 7 `.glb` asset/structure tools, current rotation/scale indicator, `Simpan Layout Map`, and `Reset Map Default`).\n      - Remove the `KeyR` shortcut that opened `ReaLuauModal` so `R` rotates objects in the Map Editor without conflict.\n   4. **Verify & Critique:**\n      - Run `npx --yes tsx --test src/game/rules.test.ts` and `compile_applet`.\n      - Restart dev server and run Playwright (`playwright-cli`) to visually verify all 3 modes (`SANDBOX TEST`, `MAP EDITOR`, `RUN MATCH`), test the quick-spawn buttons and map editor placement, inspect screenshots via `view_file`, and confirm 0 console errors.\n\n7. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Follow `<additional_user_instructions>` and `<USER_REQUEST>`: keep UI labels concise and clean, avoid unnecessary text bloat, and ensure all 3 requested modes (`SANDBOX TEST (NO NPC)`, `MAP EDITOR`, `RUN MATCH (WITH AI)`) and their exact buttons/tools work seamlessly.\n</summary>"
