  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Requirements**\n\nI\'m meticulously dissecting the user\'s request. My focus is now on the first key requirement: the three operational modes accessible through a top-bar toggle. I\'m parsing the specifics of the `PlayMode` enum/type and ensuring I understand the nuances of the `\'sandbox\'`, `\'editor\'`, and `\'match\'` options. I\'m aiming for a rock-solid, well-defined implementation.\n\n\n**Defining Sandbox Mode**\n\nMy current emphasis is on the `SANDBOX TEST` mode. I\'ve pinpointed the absolute necessity of disabling all NPCs and AI to give the player an unfettered sandbox experience, ensuring Red enemies don\'t spawn, and Blue Buddies are dormant. The core mechanics of player interaction \342\200\223 crate handling, stacking, crafting, and tank operation \342\200\223 are being prioritized for robust implementation within this mode. UI buttons for immediate object spawning are also being considered.\n\n\n**Implementing Asset Placement**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the asset placement toolbar in the sandbox. My current goal is to efficiently handle the `.glb` model placement via a side palette. I\'m focusing on the interaction; left-click places objects, right-click deletes them, and `R` rotates. I\'m prioritizing the listed assets, including different trees, wind turbines, power cores, and barricades. I\'m also planning to allow the repositioning of core arena structures.\n\n\n**Adjusting Sandbox Placement**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on fine-tuning the sandbox placement controls. I\'ve integrated rotation functionality, now mapped to the `Q` and `E` keys, with asset rotation by 45 degrees. The scaling function is mapped to `[` and `]` for easy object sizing, with a range of 0.5x to 2.5x. I\'m prioritizing the proportional height of the default trees, ensuring they are near the player\'s starting area. I\'ve also implemented map persistence buttons.\n\n\n**Refining Asset Loading**\n\nI\'m currently focused on asset loading, specifically integrating the concrete fence and barricade models. I\'ve updated the asset lists and related loading functions. I\'m also refining the tree scaling logic. I\'m working to make the trees approximately 9 units high by setting `baseHeightMult` to around `2.05 * userScale`, and scaling the foliage, or via `trunkGroup.scale.setScalar(baseHeightMult)`. I\'m going to investigate what happens to `foliageInstanced` when the trunk group\'s scale is set.\n\n\n**Optimizing Tree Scaling**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the tree scaling process in detail, zeroing in on how the trunk\'s scale affects both the trunk and the foliage. It appears that setting `trunkGroup.scale` directly scales both, ensuring that the `foliageInstanced` canopy positions and leaf sizes are proportionally adjusted. I\'m considering adjusting `uLeafScale` from `2.2` to `2.55` for a fuller canopy. I\'m now making refinements.\n\n\n**Verifying Scale Adjustments**\n\nI\'m verifying the effects of `trunkGroup.scale.setScalar(heightMult)` and a revised scaling approach. Specifically, I\'ve checked the height produced by setting `effectiveScale = refScale * 2.05 * userScale`, confirming the target height of ~9.0 units with the canopy grounded at y = 0. Furthermore, I\'ve confirmed that foliage positioning and scale are updated correctly, and now I\'m checking the contact shadow disc\'s scaling in targetGroup.\n\n\n"
