  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Asset Names**\n\nI\'ve been examining how Three.js\'s GLTFLoader impacts asset naming conventions, specifically focusing on lines like the one at 1351 of `src/game/lyoAssetsAndShaders.ts`. It seems the loader strips periods from filenames, which presents issues when checking for `.ref` file extensions, impacting how we reference assets in the game, and I need to adapt the code to account for this.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_214105"
      name: "run_command"
      arguments_json: "{\"CommandLine\":\"node -e \'\\nconst fs = require(\\\"fs\\\");\\nfor (const f of [\\\"turbine.glb\\\", \\\"power-core.glb\\\", \\\"concrete-fence-1a.glb\\\", \\\"barricade-1a.glb\\\", \\\"explosive-barrel.glb\\\", \\\"hydrant.glb\\\"]) {\\n  const buf = fs.readFileSync(\\\"public/extracted_lyo_assets/models/\\\" + f);\\n  const jsonLen = buf.readUInt32LE(12);\\n  const gltf = JSON.parse(buf.slice(20, 20 + jsonLen).toString(\\\"utf8\\\"));\\n  console.log(\\\"=== \\\" + f + \\\" === scene roots:\\\", gltf.scenes[0].nodes.map(i => i + \\\":\\\" + gltf.nodes[i].name));\\n}\\n\'\", \"Cwd\":\"/app/applet\", \"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":5000, \"toolAction\":\"Inspecting scene roots in Lyo prop GLBs\", \"toolSummary\":\"Inspect prop GLB scene roots\"}"
