  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 6
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **Current User Request:** Implement a **Low-Angle Horizon Chase Camera (Menampilkan Langit & Kanopi Pohon)** in the LYOOO Factory Playground 3D game (`src/game/FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx`, `src/game/reaConstants.ts`, `src/game/lyoAssetsAndShaders.ts`):\n     1. Replace the steep top-down gameplay camera (`y: 16.5 * zoomMult, z: 13.8 * zoomMult`) that only shows the floor.\n     2. Lower the gameplay chase camera behind and slightly above the character/tank with relative offset: **Height `Y = +5.2`**, **Back distance `Z = +12.5`**, and **`FOV = 42\302\260`** (cinematic field of view).\n     3. Point `camera.lookAt` at **`targetPos.y + 2.4`** (slightly above the character/tank head) and tilt/pan slightly toward the mouse cursor so that **~25%\342\200\22330% of the upper screen always displays the warm evening/sunset horizon sky and the purple/golden tree canopies**, while the lower screen displays tall swaying grass blades in the foreground.\n   - **Previous Completed & Verified Feature Set (Must Be Preserved):**\n     - 3-Mode Gameplay Architecture (`SANDBOX TEST (NO NPC)` default on open, `MAP EDITOR` with high top-down overview camera, and `RUN MATCH (WITH AI)`).\n     - Real extracted Lyo `.glb` assets (`player.glb`, `tree-1b.glb`, `tree-1a.glb`, `turbine.glb`, `power-core.glb`, `concrete-fence-1a.glb`, `barricade-1a.glb`, `explosive-barrel.glb`, `hydrant.glb`) and `.ktx2` textures (`game-texture.ktx2`, `tree-foliage.ktx2`).\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Completed & Verified in Prior Turns:**\n     - Fixed `.REF` node name matching (`n.endsWith(\'ref\')`) in `/src/game/lyoAssetsAndShaders.ts` (`populateRealLyoTreeFromGlb` and `spawnRealLyoPropFromGlb`) because Three.js `GLTFLoader` (`PropertyBinding.sanitizeNodeName`) strips dots (`.` -> `\"\"`, e.g. `Tree_1B.REF` becomes `Tree_1BREF`). All 9 (`tree-1b.glb`) and 8 (`tree-1a.glb`) `Tree_Foliage.*` branch canopies and `.REF` prop models now render accurately.\n     - Fixed Sandbox quick-spawn offsets and Map Editor sprite visibility (`blueBase.padSign.sprite.visible`) in `/src/game/FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx`.\n     - Verified all 3 modes in Playwright (`r4-sandbox.png`, `r4-editor.png`, `r4-match.png`) with `0` console errors.\n   - **In Progress (Just Inspected, Not Yet Edited):**\n     - Inspected `/src/game/FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx` lines 180\342\200\223460 (Scene, Camera, Lighting, Fog) and lines 2930\342\200\2233005 (Camera Follow & `lookAt` in `animate()`).\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - **Camera Math & Horizon Visibility (`src/game/FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx`):**\n     - Currently at line 412: `camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(REA_CONSTANTS.camera.fov, ...)` where `REA_CONSTANTS.camera.fov` is `35` (in `src/game/reaConstants.ts`), and `cameraZoom` is initialized to `1.22` at line 2032.\n     - Currently at lines 2942\342\200\2232996:\n       - `focusTarget` has `y: 1.0` (Buddy) or `y: 1.1` (Tank).\n       - `camOffset` in gameplay mode (`sandbox` / `match`) is `{ x: 0, y: 16.5 * zoomMult, z: 13.8 * zoomMult }`, and `camera.lookAt(finalLookX, camFollowPos.y, finalLookZ)` looks down at `y = 1.0` from `y \342\211\210 21.1`, which is a steep ~56\302\260 downward angle that hides the horizon and sky completely!\n     - With the requested **Low-Angle Horizon Chase Camera**:\n       - `FOV = 42\302\260` (`REA_CONSTANTS.camera.fov = 42`, and `applyFovMode` sets `42` for `webgl35` mode).\n       - Default `cameraZoom = 1.0` (so base offset is exact: `Y = +5.2`, `Z = +12.5`).\n       - Let `targetPos` (`focusTarget`) be `{ x: playerUnit.x, y: 0, z: playerUnit.z }` (or `{ x: mountedTank.x, y: 0.2, z: mountedTank.z }` for Tank).\n       - Camera position in gameplay (`sandbox` / `match`):\n         - `camera.position.set(camFollowPos.x + mousePanCurrent.x * 0.35 + recoilOffset.x + shakeX, (camFollowPos.y + 5.2 * zoomMult) * fovScale, camFollowPos.z + (12.5 * zoomMult) * fovScale)`\n       - Camera `lookAt` in gameplay (`sandbox` / `match`):\n         - `camera.lookAt(camFollowPos.x + mousePanCurrent.x + recoilOffset.x + shakeX, camFollowPos.y + 2.4 + mousePanCurrent.z * 0.18, camFollowPos.z + mousePanCurrent.z - 4.5)` (or looking at `(finalLookX, camFollowPos.y + 2.4 + mouseTiltY, finalLookZ)`).\n         - Wait: let\'s check the exact geometry!\n           If camera is at `(camX, targetPos.y + 5.2, targetPos.z + 12.5)` and looks at `(lookX, targetPos.y + 2.4, targetPos.z)`:\n           - `dy = 2.4 - 5.2 = -2.8`, `dz = -12.5`.\n           - Downward pitch angle is `atan(2.8 / 12.5) = 12.63\302\260`.\n           - Since vertical `FOV = 42\302\260`, the top edge of the viewport points at `+21\302\260 - 12.63\302\260 = +8.37\302\260` above horizontal, and the horizon (`0\302\260` pitch, or the distant edge of the ground plane at `z = -90..150`) sits at `(21 - 12.63) / 42 \342\211\210 20%\342\200\22328%` from the top of the screen!\n           - Even better: if `mouseNdc.y` tilts the lookAt target slightly (`+ mouseNdc.y * 0.8` on Y and `- mouseNdc.y * 2.5` on Z), moving the mouse slightly up/down tilts the camera toward the cursor while keeping ~25%\342\200\22330% of the top of the screen showing the warm evening sky horizon and the purple/golden tree canopies!\n     - **Sky Horizon & Ground Plane Check (`src/game/FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx` lines 408\342\200\223620):**\n       - We must inspect lines 460\342\200\223640 of `src/game/FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx` to see how the ground plane, sky dome/gradient, and distant horizon are built!\n       - Specifically: if the green ground plane extends too far or if `scene.background` is flat `#9ad9ea`, then looking at the horizon won\'t show a **warm evening sky horizon (\"horizon langit sore hangat\")** unless we have a proper warm sunset/afternoon sky dome / horizon gradient shader (e.g., warm golden-peach/amber-violet horizon blending into soft sky above) and an appropriate ground size + fog distance so the top 25%\342\200\22330% of the viewport clearly shows the warm evening sky & distant hills/horizon framed by the purple and gold Lyo tree canopies, while the foreground at the bottom of the screen shows tall swaying `InfiniteGrass` blades!\n       - Also check `Blue HQ` at `(0, 18.5)`: when the player spawns at `(0, 11.5)` and the camera is at `z = 11.5 + 12.5 = 24.0` at height `y = 5.2`, `Blue HQ` at `(0, 18.5)` is right between `z = 11.5` and `z = 24.0`!\n       - **CRITICAL CAMERA OCCLUSION INSIGHT:**\n         Look at `Blue HQ`\'s position in `DEFAULT_MAP_LAYOUT`:\n         - Player spawns at `(0, 11.5)`.\n         - `blueHq` is at `{ x: 0, z: 18.5 }` (which is `4.2` units tall, `7.6` units wide, sitting directly at `z = 18.5` between the player at `z = 11.5` and the low-angle camera at `z = 24.0, y = 5.2`!).\n         - If `blueHq` stays at `(0, 18.5)` directly behind the player at `z = 11.5`, a low-angle camera at `(0, 5.2, 24.0)` looking at `(0, 2.4, 11.5)` will have its line of sight blocked or crowded by the back wall of `Blue HQ`!\n         - Let\'s check where `blueHq` should be placed or if `blueHq` should be placed to the side (e.g. `x: 7.5, z: 14.5`, opposite `bluePad` at `x: -6.8, z: 14.5`) OR behind the camera / transparent when occluding, OR if the player spawns at `(0, 10.5)` in front of `blueHq` at `(-8.5, 16.5)`!\n         - Moving `blueHq` to `{ x: 7.2, z: 15.0 }` (right side of the road, symmetric with `bluePad` at `{ x: -6.8, z: 13.5 }` on the left side of the road) AND adding Purple & Gold Lyo Trees along the horizon/road edges ensures that the camera at `(0, 5.2, 23.0)` has a completely unobstructed view of the player Buddy/Tank on the dirt road, flanked by tall swaying grass in the foreground, the Stacking Pad on the left, Blue HQ on the right, and the lush purple/gold tree canopies against the warm evening horizon sky in the top 25%\342\200\22330% of the screen!\n\n4. **Errors & Fixes**\n   - **Resolved Error 1:** `Tree_1B.REF` and `WindTurbine.REF` were not matched by `n.endsWith(\'.ref\') || n.endsWith(\'_ref\')` because Three.js `GLTFLoader` sanitizes node names by removing `.` (`Tree_1BREF`). Fixed in `/src/game/lyoAssetsAndShaders.ts` by matching `n.endsWith(\'ref\')`.\n   - **Resolved Error 2:** `TypeError: Cannot set properties of undefined (setting \'visible\')` when hiding the pad sign in editor mode because the property on `blueBase` is `blueBase.padSign.sprite`, not `blueBase.padStatusSprite`. Fixed in `/src/game/FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx`.\n   - **Resolved Note:** HMR is disabled in this environment; always call `restart_dev_server` after `compile_applet` before running Playwright verification so Vite serves the latest code.\n\n5. **Active Context**\n   - Dev server is running on `http://localhost:3000`.\n   - All existing unit tests (`npm test`) and TypeScript build (`compile_applet`) pass.\n\n6. **Next Steps**\n   1. **Inspect lines 450\342\200\223660 of `/src/game/FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx`, `/src/game/reaConstants.ts`, and `/src/game/lyoAssetsAndShaders.ts`:**\n      - Check how the sky/fog/lighting (`day` / warm afternoon preset), ground mesh, `DEFAULT_MAP_LAYOUT`, and `InfiniteGrass` blade height (`createLyoInfiniteGrassSystem`) are configured.\n   2. **Update Camera Constants & Chase Camera Logic (`/src/game/reaConstants.ts` & `/src/game/FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx`):**\n      - Set `REA_CONSTANTS.camera.fov = 42` (`42\302\260` cinematic FOV).\n      - Set default `cameraZoom = 1.0` in `FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx` so gameplay camera offset is exact (`Y = +5.2`, `Z = +12.5`).\n      - In `animate()` (when `currentPlayMode !== \'editor\'` and `state !== \'title\'`, and also update `\'title\'` camera to match the low-angle cinematic showcase):\n        - Position camera at relative offset **`Y = +5.2 * zoomMult`**, **`Z = +12.5 * zoomMult`** behind the player/tank (`targetPos`).\n        - Set `camera.lookAt` to **`targetPos.y + 2.4`** (slightly above the character/tank head) and tilt/pan slightly toward the mouse cursor (`mousePanCurrent.x`, `mousePanCurrent.z` / `mouseNdc`), so **25%\342\200\22330% of the upper viewport always shows the warm evening sky horizon and purple/gold tree canopies**.\n        - Keep `MAP EDITOR` mode (`currentPlayMode === \'editor\'`) using its high top-down overview camera (`y: 54.0 * editorZoom, z: 22.0 * editorZoom`) so map editing remains effortless.\n   3. **Enhance Warm Evening Sky Horizon & Foreground Tall Grass (`src/game/FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx` & `src/game/lyoAssetsAndShaders.ts`):**\n      - Add a warm evening/sunset sky dome shader (`SkyHorizonDome`: warm golden-amber/coral-peach lower horizon `#ffbe7b` -> `#ff8e6e` blending into soft twilight-sky `#79a6d2` / `#5d6db0` above, plus soft warm directional sunlight `#ffe6c2` and atmospheric horizon fog `#f5b076`) so the top 25%\342\200\22330% of the viewport displays a gorgeous warm afternoon/evening horizon sky behind the purple (`#5e57a5` -> `#775cf6`) and golden (`#eab308` -> `#facc15`) Lyo tree canopies.\n      - Ensure `Blue HQ` (`x: 7.4, z: 14.5`) and `Red HQ` (`x: -7.4, z: -18.5`) sit cleanly alongside the central road (never blocking the low-angle camera behind the player at `(0, 11.5)`), and place Lyo purple/gold trees along the road & horizon so their canopies frame the upper 25%\342\200\22330% sky horizon.\n      - Tune `InfiniteGrass` blade height/scale near the camera in `src/game/lyoAssetsAndShaders.ts` so lush tall grass blades are prominently visible in the bottom foreground of the low-angle camera.\n   4. **Verify via Unit Tests, Compilation, Dev Server Restart, and Playwright Visual Check:**\n      - Run `compile_applet` and `restart_dev_server`.\n      - Open `http://localhost:3000` in Playwright (`1440x900`), capture screenshots of `SANDBOX TEST (NO NPC)`, `MAP EDITOR`, and `RUN MATCH (WITH AI)`, inspect the screenshots with `view_file` to confirm ~25%\342\200\22330% upper horizon sky + purple tree canopies and lower foreground tall grass, and verify `0` console errors.\n\n7. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Keep the UI clean and in Indonesian as established; do not add unrequested telemetry or debug overlays.\n   - Always verify visual changes in a real headless Chromium browser via `playwright-cli` and `view_file` on captured screenshots before finishing.\n</summary>"
